theorem.raw:
\label{tm34}
The operators $\delta_x,\delta_y, \mathcal Z$ and
$\overline{D}$ generate a Lie algebra of linear operators on the
space of all functions from $\mathbb{Z}^2$ into $\mathbb C$. The Lie
bracket is $[A,B]=AB-BA$ and the relations on the generators are

\begin{align}
\label{id1}
[\delta_x,\mathcal{Z}]&=1+\delta_x,\\
[\delta_y,\mathcal{Z}]&= i(1+\delta_y+\delta_y^2),\\
\label{id3}
[\overline{D},\mathcal{Z}]&=\left(\frac{1+i}{2}+\frac{i}{2}\delta_y\right)\overline{D},\\
[\overline{D},\delta_x]&=[\overline{D},\delta_y]=[\delta_x,\delta_y]=0.
\label{id2}
\end{align}

